WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.750
The concept of a forward
market is based on

2
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.700
participants facilitating
the purchase

3
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.760
and sale of products that
will not be produced or

4
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.110
won't be available until

5
00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.375
some specific time in the future.

6
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:33.760
In general, whether
you're a speculator

7
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.385
willing to assume risk in
order to make a profit,

8
00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:38.110
or you're an investor
who's adopting

9
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:41.005
a hedging strategy to
protect a position,

10
00:00:41.005 --> 00:00:44.770
futures allow you to lock
into prevailing prices.

11
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.890
The forward or future price
must take into account

12
00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.350
multiple factors that can
influence the price of

13
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.260
the product and the structure
of the end product,

14
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.765
whether physical or
purely financial,

15
00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:59.515
must be clearly specified
in the contract.

16
00:00:59.515 --> 00:01:01.580
Over many decades,
exchange traded

17
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.990
futures contracts have grown

18
00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.300
into popular investment vehicle.

19
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.990
Any futures market is based
on some underlying product,

20
00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.120
often a physical commodity and

21
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.370
offer producers and
end users the ability

22
00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.935
to hedge against
adverse price movements

23
00:01:15.935 --> 00:01:18.245
in the value of the end product.

24
00:01:18.245 --> 00:01:20.210
Some other products available on

25
00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.310
global futures markets include

26
00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.635
metals such as gold and silver.

27
00:01:24.635 --> 00:01:26.675
Energy-related products such as

28
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:28.555
crude oil and natural gas.

29
00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.500
Grains such as corn,

30
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.000
soy beans, and rice.

31
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.100
Soft commodities such as coffee,

32
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.070
cocoa, sugar, and frozen
concentrated orange juice,

33
00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.085
as well as financial products,
including interest rates,

34
00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:42.680
currencies, and equity indices,

35
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.620
among several others in
each of these category.

36
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.720
Sellers of these
products may wish to

37
00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.400
lock into as higher prices as

38
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.930
possible to make sure

39
00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:53.450
that at least they make
a profit at the minimum,

40
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.495
or at worst, that they cover
the cost of production.

41
00:01:56.495 --> 00:01:58.520
While end users may wish to hedge

42
00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.860
against rising prices
in order to ensure

43
00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.110
a reasonable price
for any commodity and

44
00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.575
control as best they
can the cost they face.

45
00:02:06.575 --> 00:02:09.260
The more producers,
buyers and sellers and

46
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.080
hedgers that interact
in any futures market,

47
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.200
the more speculators
are drawn in.

48
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.490
Creating additional liquidity and

49
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.345
generally improving
market conditions.

50
00:02:19.345 --> 00:02:22.190
In this module we'll
introduce you to some of

51
00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:25.010
the risks faced by investors
in the futures market.

52
00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.125
How certain of those
risks are mitigated,

53
00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:28.730
as well as the difference between

54
00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.395
spot and forward prices,

55
00:02:30.395 --> 00:02:32.995
and contango and backwardation.

56
00:02:32.995 --> 00:02:35.270
We'll also provide you
with other insights

57
00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.490
about the mechanics
of trading futures,

58
00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.635
including the roles of
commoditized contracts,

59
00:02:40.635 --> 00:02:42.865
as well as margin requirements.

60
00:02:42.865 --> 00:02:53.140
Come back and join us.